      "node_id": "kg_doc_5",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "A pre-commissioning unit (PRECOMMUNIT) or (PCU) is used by the United States Navy to describe vessels under construction prior to their official commissioning. For example, prior to its commissioning, the aircraft carrier \"Gerald R. Ford\" (CVN-78) has been described by the Navy as \"pre-commissioning unit (PCU) \"Gerald R. Ford\" .\" However, \"PCU\" is only a descriptive term and is not a prefix or a part of the ship's official name. Until they are commissioned, U.S. Navy vessels are officially identified by their given name and hull number only with no prefix, such as \"Gerald R. Ford\" (CVN-78).",
      "depth": 0,
